course: dictionary
lesson: 2513
title: Things that only seem true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deceptively is an adverb. It tells you how something seems, and the seeming is not the truth. «The question looks deceptively easy.» At first glance it seems easy, but it hides a trick, so you must read it carefully.
explain: Look for clue words near the word: looks, seems, appears, at first glance. They tell you that the appearance and the reality are different. Test your meaning by swapping in "seems but really is": «The question seems but really is easy» does not fit, so think again and read the whole sentence.
explain: In a house advert, «a deceptively spacious flat» looks small from the street, but it is bigger inside than you would expect. The word warns you that the outside does not show the full picture.
fact: Deceptively is an adverb, so it describes how something seems or is.
fact: «Deceptively» means in a way that makes something seem different from what it really is.
fact: «Deceptively simple» means a problem looks easy but has a hidden trick, so read carefully.
fact: In house adverts, «deceptively spacious» means the house is bigger inside than it looks from outside.
fact: A «deceptively calm» sea looks safe, but it warns the reader that danger may be hidden.
exercise: «The puzzle looks deceptively easy.» What does deceptively mean here? | It is written in pencil | *It seems easy but is really harder than it looks | It is very easy and clear all the way through | It is so easy that it bores everyone
exercise: Ruby says a maths problem is «deceptively simple». What is her warning? | The problem has missing numbers | It is a question about shapes | *Read it carefully, because there is a hidden trick | Skip it, because it is too long
exercise: An advert says «a deceptively spacious flat». What does it mean? | It is painted in bright colours | It has no windows | It is very small and cramped inside | *It is bigger inside than it looks from outside
test: «The sea looked deceptively calm, but the boat soon rocked.» What does the story warn the reader? | The sea is always gentle | Stay on the beach all day | *Be careful, because the calm may hide danger | Swim as fast as you can
test: Which word is closest in meaning to deceptively in «the box looks deceptively light»? | Brightly | *Misleadingly | Quickly | Carefully
exam: «The question looked deceptively easy, so Sam read it twice.» Why did Sam read the question twice? | Because he had finished early and wanted to check | Because the paper was too small to read | *Because it looked easy but hid a trick | Because he could not see the page
